          "id": "docs/shell/configuration/ide-integration_public.md_chunk_6",
          "score": 0.8282666,
          "content": "When you run Bob Shell inside Bob IDE's integrated terminal, it automatically detects the environment and offers to set up integration:\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ \u003e Do you want to connect Bob IDE to Bob Shell?                               │\n│ If you select Yes, we'll install an extension that allows the CLI to ac ... │\n│                                                                             │\n│   1. Yes                                                                    │\n|   2. No                                                                     │\n|   3. No, don't ask again                                                    │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\nSelecting \"Yes\" will:\n\n1. Install the Bob Shell Companion extension\n2. Configure the necessary connection settings\n3. Establish the connection automatically",
          "metadata": {
            "section_path": "Integrating with Bob IDE \u003e Installation methods \u003e Method 1: Automatic setup (recommended)"
          },
          "rerank_score": 0.9973061
        },
        {
          "id": "docs/shell/core-concepts/tools_public.md_chunk_5",
          "score": 15.156155,
          "content": "Run commands and perform system operations in your terminal.\n\nThe `execute_command` tool runs CLI commands in your workspace, such as installing dependencies, running tests, and building projects.\n**When Bob Shell uses command tools:** When you ask Bob Shell to run commands, install packages, run scripts, or complete system operations.",
          "metadata": {
            "section_path": "Tools \u003e Tool categories \u003e Command tools"
          },
          "rerank_score": 0.9759006
