        {
          "id": "docs/shell/index_public.md_chunk_8",
          "score": 10.426897,
          "content": "Ready to bring AI assistance to your terminal? Follow these steps to get up and running:\n\n1. Install Bob Shell on your system. For more information, see [Installing and setting up Bob Shell](/docs/shell/getting-started/install-and-setup).\n2. Launch your first interactive session. For more information, see [Starting Bob Shell interactively](/docs/shell/getting-started/start-bobshell-interactive).\n3. Review the security guidelines to minimize potential security risks. For more information, see [Security guidelines](/docs/ide/security/bob-security-guidance).\n\n**Note:**\nStart by using Bob Shell for a task you're already familiar with. This helps you understand how Bob Shell interprets commands and provides assistance in a terminal context.",
          "metadata": {
            "section_path": "Welcome to Bob Shell \u003e Getting started with Bob Shell"
          },
          "rerank_score": 0.9748691
        },
        {
          "id": "docs/shell/getting-started/start-bobshell-non-interactive_public.md_chunk_1",
          "score": 0.8181839,
          "content": "1. Open a new terminal window.\n\n2. Navigate to the main directory of your project.\n\n3. Run the `bob -p` command to start Bob Shell in your terminal.\n\n**Note:**\nBefore starting a non-interactive session for the first time, you must accept the license agreement. You can do this by either:\n- Running the following command in your terminal: `bob --accept-license -p \"Explain this project\"`\n- Starting Bob Shell with an interactive session first to review and accept the license.\n\n**Note:**\nFor non-interactive sessions, you need to use the API key authentication method instead of the IBMid authentication. For more information, see [Installing](/docs/shell/getting-started/install-and-setup#api-key-authentication).\n\nFor example:\n\n```bash\nbob -p \"Explain this project\"\n```",
          "metadata": {
            "section_path": "Starting a non-interactive session \u003e To start a non-interactive session:"
          },
          "rerank_score": 0.93318766
        },
        {
          "id": "docs/shell/configuration/custom-modes-bobshell_public.md_chunk_19",
          "score": 12.468235,
          "content": "When migrating custom modes from Bob IDE to Bob Shell:\n\nThe Visual interface with panels aspect of Bob IDE provides UI interaction, supports in-editor diffs and previews for file editing, includes an integrated terminal for command running, allows mode switching via UI dropdown or slash commands, and offers both settings UI and files for configuration.\nThe Terminal-based interface aspect of Bob Shell provides UI interaction, supports CLI diff view or external editor for file editing, includes direct shell running for command running, allows mode switching via slash commands or CLI arguments, and offers configuration files only for configuration.",
          "metadata": {
            "section_path": "Custom modes \u003e Migrating modes from Bob IDE \u003e Key differences"
          },
          "rerank_score": 0.9323302
        }
      ]
